<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Closure of the Neoplatonic Academy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">529 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The closure of the Neoplatonic Academy refers to the Byzantine emperor Justinian's measures in 529 CE that ended pagan philosophical teaching in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>. Several of the displaced philosophers travelled to the court of the Sasanian king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a>. The episode illustrates the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a>'s interest in Greek learning.</p></div>
